    "scope": "Three useful Commons2005 front,2024 drum/dome and2021 rear exterior pictures plus standard viewer PMTiles/DEM. Reference photos viewed only, not downloaded or redistributed. No bespoke surveys/plans researched.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mdinakathedraal.jpg",
        "author": "Cicero (per Commons description/copyright attribution)",
        "date": "2005-08",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0 / GFDL-1.2-or-later",
        "observed": "Inspected west front: symmetrical warm limestone Baroque facade with two clock towers, open arched belfries and curved decorated stone spires/crosses. Broad central triangular pediment, two main storeys with paired pilasters/capitals, three dark wooden rectangular doors under segmental/triangular surrounds. Upper central tall arched multi-pane window, oval relief over central door, shallow steps across facade. Fine carving, clock markings and sculptural details are simplified."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Paul%27s_Cathedral_Dome,_Mdina.jpg",
        "author": "Godwin Borg",
        "date": "2024-07-26",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected close exterior dome/drum view: tall polygonal limestone drum, large round arched gridded window between paired corner pilasters, layered cornice, low curved warm weathered metal canopy with stone ribs/scrolls, small polygonal lantern with dark glazing and tiny cross/finial. Roof materials/colors use approximate shared surfaces; no photo texture copied."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mdina_cathedral.jpg",
        "author": "Marika Caruana",
        "date": "2021-07-02",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected rear twilight exterior: prominent octagonal windowed drum and low dark weathered metal dome with stone scroll ribs, small top lantern/cross; twin front belfries/spires to the west. Broad main body has simple high wall and flat/very low roof lines; lower adjoining urban buildings and bastions obscure ground/rear joins. Twilight floodlight color is not baked into the model. Exact rear windows/urban neighbors/plateau terrain remain approximate or excluded."
      }
    ]
